### Step 1 — Scope

Step 1 is interactive Q&A and is never skipped. It authors ONE kind of knowledge — what is
wanted, in the user's terms — and lands it in ONE artifact: `wave-NN-<slug>.requirements.md`,
beside the spec under `specs/epic-NN-<slug>/`. Numbered requirements, each with its
`provenance:` and its acceptance criteria; then "Not Doing". No design, no tasks, no evals.

**At wave and epic scale the requirements sit under their themes.** Three to six `## <theme>`
sections, each opening on one sentence that says what the run is for in that respect, with the
`### REQ-<n>` headings under them; never a flat `## Requirements` list, which the governing-skill
hook refuses. The themes are the run's goals: the situation report prints one goal line per
theme, its criteria discharged and its open REQs read from the matrix, so a theme is never typed
into the plan's `goals:` line, which carries measured goals only. The `## Goal` paragraph names
the themes, so the card's Purpose lists them.

**Write every criterion so a "fails when" is nameable.** Step 2 has to be able to say what
planted defect would turn each criterion's eval red; a criterion that admits no such sentence
("the code is clean", "performance is good") cannot be evaluated and is rewritten here, where
it is still cheap. That is a Step-1 quality bar, not a Step-2 discovery.

**The step ends at the card below, rendered in full.** One line per requirement, never a
paragraph — the artifact path is the depth, and `explain <requirement>` opens one. Approval
is against the card, and the card's own question is the gate.

```
Step 1 · Requirements

  Purpose
    <one paragraph: what this run ships, and for whom>

  Requirements
    REQ-<id> <the requirement in one line> · provenance <user quote | spec section | ticket  ACs <n>
             | report>

  Not Doing
    <one line per excluded item — what is out, and why>

  Inherited  <n> inherited · <a> adopted · <c> carried · <k> closed · listed in <file>#Deferrals

  Artifacts
    requirements  <docs-root>/specs/epic-NN-<slug>/wave-NN-<slug>.requirements.md

Do you approve these requirements? Reply "approved" to approve it.
explain <requirement> · set <flag>=<value>
```

Card: `bash <plugin-root>/scripts/card.sh step1 <requirements.md>` renders it whole; no stdin.

The card prints one `Inherited` line of counts over the newest continuation's `deferred:` and `debt:` lines, never the lines. The requirements file's `## Inherited deferrals` disposes of each deferral with one of `adopted: <id> as REQ-<n>`, `again: <id>` (carried) or `closed: <id> <reason>`; a disposal naming an id the continuation lacks refuses the card.

Right after the card, run `session-poker.sh debt adopt <newest continuation>`: it writes each carried `debt:` item into this run's ledger, once, with its touches kept.

**Evidence:** `Step 1: requirements: <path>; <how the scope was approved>`

